IMPORT `il43-nouns`

-- Row il-43. THE CITATIONS, as typed values.
-- A citation is encoded as TWO descriptions: what the citing words say they point at, and what the target is. A test compares them. Where they differ, the citation does not point at what it says;
-- that is a defect, kept in an expected-red file with its count declared in check.sh and encoding.json.
-- Four citations are recorded. One is a defect: the definition of "a suspended permit", which s 1יג(ד)(2) of the Foreign Workers Law takes from s 223א of the National Insurance Law, was deleted from s 223א.
-- Three are sound and are here as controls: the two other terms cited in the same sentence of s 1יג(ד)(2), and the citation in s 2(א1)(1) of the same Law to s 398(א2)(5) of the National Insurance Law.
-- LIMBS. Limb (a) is the question whether the target is as the citing words say; limb (b) is the question whether the citing words still read so in the latest official text of the citing provision.
-- Each limb says where it was read from: the official instrument (a Sefer HaChukim page image) or the consolidation only (the Hebrew Wikisource text, which is not official).
-- A date for which the sources held give no answer is NOTHING; there is no REFUSE.

§ `Cross-references`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citation points at what it says` MEANS c's `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS c's `the target is`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs were read from the official instruments` MEANS
    c's `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    AND c's `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

-- Whether the target stands in the official text on a day. The only answer the sources held give is the day it was deleted and the days from then on; for any earlier day, and for a target
-- with no recorded deletion, the answer is NOTHING (no source held says when the target was added, or that it was never deleted).
GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the target stands in the official text on` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the target was deleted from the official text on`
        WHEN JUST deleted THEN IF day AT LEAST deleted THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

